# The release that last needed setup re-run on every device.
#
# Most releases are files, packages and units, and the updater handles those on its own.
# A release that changes something owned by init.sh instead - a desktop shortcut, a cron
# entry, an autostart line, a font - puts its own version here. The updater compares this
# against var/init_ran_for and runs setup once when they differ, with nobody present.
#
# Leave it alone for a release that does not need it. Bumping it for a release that
# changes nothing in setup costs every device a pointless run.
